From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 09:03:06 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] droidcamsrc: keep the raw preview running while the recorder
 records

Starting a recording with the external recorder connects the camera to two
more clients: CameraSource connects to it when droidmedia creates the
recorder, and starting the recording reconnects droidmedia's own camera
through the recording proxy (Camera::RecordingProxy::startRecording()). Each
connect makes the API1 camera service reset its preview callback flag to
CAMERA_FRAME_CALLBACK_FLAG_NOOP (CameraClient::connect()).

When the viewfinder uses raw preview data, the frames come through that
callback, so the viewfinder froze on its last frame for as long as the
recording ran, while vidsrc kept delivering encoded frames. Seen on the HP
TouchPad (msm8660 HAL1, Halium 16 GSI): 15 viewfinder frames per second
before start-capture, none until stop-capture, 15 again afterwards.

The flag was already set again after stopping a recording ("seems to be
overwritten"); set it again after starting one as well.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 gst/droidcamsrc/gstdroidcamsrcdev.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/gst/droidcamsrc/gstdroidcamsrcdev.c b/gst/droidcamsrc/gstdroidcamsrcdev.c
--- a/gst/droidcamsrc/gstdroidcamsrcdev.c
+++ b/gst/droidcamsrc/gstdroidcamsrcdev.c
@@ -1012,6 +1012,14 @@
 
   ret = TRUE;
 
+  /* Starting the recording connects the camera to a second client and back:
+   * CameraSource connects to it, and its start reconnects droidmedia's camera
+   * through the recording proxy. Each connect resets the camera service's
+   * preview callback flag to NOOP, so with raw preview the viewfinder got no
+   * frames until the recording ended. Set the flag again, as is done after
+   * stopping. */
+  gst_droidcamsrc_dev_update_preview_callback_flag (dev);
+
   /* Send the preview image out if requested. */
   if (src->post_preview)
     gst_droidcamsrc_dev_post_preview (dev);
